    "result_text": "Done. Only one test class exists in the repo (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily owner-creation limit: creating an owner is now rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already have today's `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the per-city capacity gate), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today; throws `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` when the count is \u2265 100 (`DAILY_LIMIT`).\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 checked exception so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 responds `429` with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other handlers.\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `escalation/...DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step into `rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (after `checkCityCapacity`, before `build`), under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\nThe check reads the repository (no request body binding), so it doesn't consume the single `@RequestBody` read, and it runs before the entity is built/saved.",
